            <ArticleTitle>Can life-style changes reverse coronary atherosclerosis?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>123-6, 129-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>&quot;It seemed to me that bypass surgery had become a metaphor for an incomplete approach to coronary heart disease: bypassing the problem without also dealing with the underlying causes.... What would happen if those causes were addressed more directly?&quot; The author goes on to describe an intensive risk-modification regimen to arrest or even reverse progression of atherosclerosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
